  :seon.task/plan "Root, 2026-11-15 01:10, from Stage 0 [M]: a merge of main into a branch with conflicts applies nothing (owner: \"The merge doesn't happen while there are conflicts\"), so while a branch is conflicted it holds none of main's clean datoms. my.branch/resolve! then writes a side onto the branch as it stands, and what that write sets off (a task's contract read on the whole entity) is judged on a state that never exists once merged: context-4's resolve! of a [:task ...] side failed :seon.task/execution missing, because main's fact was not yet on the branch. Change: resolve! records each entry's chosen side only (as resolve-tx marks it, with its side); the next merge-main builds the candidate (main plus the branch's own datoms, each conflict at its chosen side, seon.merge/side-tx) and writes it in one transaction when every entry is decided, so each resolution is checked on the result it makes and no merge happens while one is open. Deletes: resolve!'s immediate side write (side-tx stays as the candidate's writer). Estimate: one merge-main (O(the branch's writes)) a resolution round, not one write a key. Proof, red first: a conflicted task entry resolved to main's side, where main also set an attribute the branch lacks, merges with the task valid under its contract. Proof as root states it (2026-11-15): a branch whose task lacks a key main holds (:seon.task/execution) resolves a [:task ...] conflict :theirs in one transaction, and the entity passes its contract; red today: execution missing."
