 {:seon.task/name "a-session-lands-through-seon-done", :seon.task/plan "Plan item 18 of docs/plan.md#the-order (data, runtime): bin/land goes, with the bridge, landed-tx and bin/prove --out, onto seon_done: a Claude session lands as a Seon agent does, its branch merged by the one :merge (seon.merge/one-merge-system, landing 10), git following the store by the write-back. PRIOR WORK: bin/land (the shell path every session lands by today; its header says where it deviates from a thin wrapper), seon_done and the writer's :merge (landing 10), the pilot (plan item 14, a-merge-moves-gits-main-to-the-stores-files in seon.source). Each check bin/land makes in shell (Completes, dropped entries, Deletes, the estimate, health, the laws) is the merge's data first (landing 10); then bin/land is a thin wrapper over the op, then deleted once the pilot carries a week of landings. Proof: a session's change lands through seon_done end to end, git's main moved to the store's files.", :seon.task/kind :work, :seon.task/needs #{"seon.source/a-merge-moves-gits-main-to-the-stores-files" "seon.merge/one-merge-system"}, :seon.task/proofs #{seon.server-test/a-sessions-change-lands-through-done}, :seon.task/estimate {seon.writer/merge {:n 200, :order :linear, :ticks 200000000, :bytes 800000000}}}
